The Heat (Diffusion) Equation in the Spatial Domain:\frac{\partial u}{\partial t} = \alpha^2 \frac{\partial^2 u}{\partial x^2} \quad \text{or} \quad u_t = \alpha^2 u_{xx}

where u(t,x) is the temperature distribution in time and space,\alpha is the thermal diffusivity constant.

Apply the Fourier transform in space:\mathcal{F}(u(t, x)) = \hat{u}(t,\omega)

.

